WEBVTT

00:01.177 --> 00:02.307
<i>Satisfy</i>,

00:02.787 --> 00:06.257
a virtual reality game 
often called "another Earth."

00:07.707 --> 00:11.147
Today, we'll be talking 
with our guests about

00:11.147 --> 00:15.707
what makes each job special 
and the importance of classes.

00:16.077 --> 00:22.677
It's said that your class has a huge 
influence on your strength in <i>Satisfy</i>.

00:22.677 --> 00:26.007
What are your thoughts, Yura-san?

00:26.257 --> 00:27.577
That's true.

00:27.937 --> 00:31.737
There are definitely 
advantages to certain jobs.

00:29.487 --> 00:35.017
<b><b>Yura</b></b>

00:29.487 --> 00:35.017
<b><b>Black Mage</b></b>

00:29.487 --> 00:35.017
<b><b>Total Rank: 5</b></b>

00:29.487 --> 00:35.017
<b>m 0 0 l 80 0 80 8 0 8</b>

00:29.487 --> 00:35.017
<b>m 0 0 l 95 0 95 8 0 8</b>

00:31.737 --> 00:35.017
But it's also important to master a job.

00:35.937 --> 00:41.127
You say that, but you're actually jealous 
of people with special class jobs.

00:38.287 --> 00:43.147
<b><b>Roy</b></b>

00:38.287 --> 00:43.147
<b><b>Blood Warrior</b></b>

00:38.287 --> 00:43.147
<b><b>Total Rank: 53</b></b>

00:38.287 --> 00:43.147
<b>m 0 0 l 145 0 145 8 0 8</b>

00:38.287 --> 00:43.147
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 8 0 8</b>

00:41.127 --> 00:44.317
You're just a Black Mage.

00:44.317 --> 00:47.017
In this game, rare trumps normal.

00:47.017 --> 00:49.167
And epic trumps rare!

00:49.167 --> 00:51.407
It's all about how high your numbers are.

00:51.867 --> 00:53.557
As proof...

00:55.157 --> 00:56.987
H-His sword!

00:58.877 --> 01:04.637
I shot up to the top 100 once 
I switched to an epic class.

01:05.927 --> 01:08.897
A Blood Warrior's special ability

01:08.897 --> 01:11.927
is to drain their opponent's 
HP as a passive skill.

01:11.927 --> 01:14.347
Oh? You know of it?

01:14.347 --> 01:17.677
So you basically rely on your job, huh?

01:17.677 --> 01:19.477
Just like you rely on your items?

01:19.477 --> 01:20.897
What did you say?

01:20.897 --> 01:26.547
Th-There are currently said to 
be three epic jobs in <i>Satisfy</i>.

01:26.547 --> 01:30.267
One is Roy-san's job, Blood Warrior.

01:30.267 --> 01:34.577
The second is the job used 
by the #7 player, Agnus,

01:34.577 --> 01:37.167
but he's asked that the 
details be kept secret.

01:37.167 --> 01:42.727
As for the third... There's no information
about who it could even be!

01:42.727 --> 01:45.417
Of course, there are also said to be

01:45.417 --> 01:48.927
rare and normal jobs that 
don't rely on combat...

01:48.927 --> 01:55.597
But which users, and which jobs, will 
change the history of <i>Satisfy</i> forever?

01:55.597 --> 01:58.467
We'll have to watch and see!

02:20.267 --> 02:21.797
<b>Overgeared</b>

02:21.797 --> 02:25.027
<b>Overgeared</b>

03:31.487 --> 03:34.297
I'm glad you got out of 
the hospital so fast.

03:34.297 --> 03:39.747
Yeah. If there are still young kids like 
you out there, this world isn't so bad.

03:39.747 --> 03:43.287
Without me, you couldn't even 
have gone to the doctor.

03:43.287 --> 03:44.697
Yeah.

03:44.697 --> 03:49.087
Of course, after I helped you, 
you want to give me it, right?

03:49.087 --> 03:50.407
Yeah.

03:52.547 --> 03:54.897
W-Wait. That's the one
 thing I can't give you.

03:54.897 --> 03:55.967
What?!

03:55.967 --> 03:57.747
But I saved your life!

03:57.747 --> 04:00.367
You would've died if it wasn't for me!

04:00.367 --> 04:01.707
Please understand.

04:01.707 --> 04:04.727
That's a family treasure, 
passed down for generations.

04:04.957 --> 04:06.267
Family treasure?

04:06.587 --> 04:11.777
Dainsleif and Valhalla 
were made by my ancestor.

04:11.777 --> 04:16.527
For years, no one has been 
able to draw out their power.

04:16.947 --> 04:21.377
But 130 years ago, a man appeared.

04:21.377 --> 04:22.967
His name was Pagma.

04:23.357 --> 04:26.867
Not only was he able to 
understand their abilities,

04:26.867 --> 04:29.777
but he danced beautifully with them.

04:29.777 --> 04:33.327
But he left without taking them.

04:34.087 --> 04:38.917
All he said was that their true 
owner would appear someday.

04:40.887 --> 04:43.297
Hey! That must be me!

04:43.297 --> 04:45.387
I'm Pagma's Successor, after all!

04:47.097 --> 04:48.367
Yes...

04:49.407 --> 04:52.567
You were able to use them...

04:54.117 --> 04:58.027
But if you're really Pagma's Successor,

04:58.497 --> 05:01.037
you must prove the legend true.

05:01.927 --> 05:02.637
<b></b>Job Quest

05:01.927 --> 05:02.637
<b><b>Pagma's Successor</b></b>

05:01.927 --> 05:02.637
<b><b>has been created</b></b>

05:02.097 --> 05:03.287
<i>System guidance.</i>

05:03.367 --> 05:06.787
<i>A legendary job quest has been generated.</i>

05:06.787 --> 05:08.577
<i>"Prove the Legend."</i>

05:06.847 --> 05:10.787
<b></b>Job Quest
<b>Prove the Legend</b>

Gather all the legends of Pagma
using his Sword Dance as a clue.
Details will be updated as the quest proceeds.


*No time limit
*Once a legendary job quest has begun,
job cannot be changed


Clear Condition: Complete all associated quests.
Clear Reward: Unknown
*Acquired after each quest is completed.

05:06.847 --> 05:10.787
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 58 0 58</b>

05:08.577 --> 05:12.767
<i>This is a multi-part quest involving 
the legendary blacksmith Pagma.</i>

05:12.767 --> 05:17.437
<i>Completing all parts will give you 
the power to change the world.</i>

05:17.857 --> 05:20.257
<i>That's a crazy reward...</i>

05:21.027 --> 05:21.757
<b></b>Job Quest

05:21.027 --> 05:21.757
<b><b>Pagma's Successor</b></b>

05:21.027 --> 05:21.757
<b><b>will now begin</b></b>

05:21.277 --> 05:24.587
<i>So I get this sword and armor someday?</i>

05:24.587 --> 05:26.267
<i>In that case...</i>

05:26.267 --> 05:28.087
<i>Give 'em to me now!</i>

05:28.087 --> 05:30.517
What's with that pathetic face?

05:30.517 --> 05:33.897
I figured you were lying about 
being Pagma's Successor.

05:33.897 --> 05:35.017
What?!

05:35.017 --> 05:37.567
Fine, then! I'll show you my skill!

05:37.567 --> 05:39.637
Teach me how to be a blacksmith already!

05:39.637 --> 05:42.837
Jeez, you're sure in a hurry.

05:43.287 --> 05:46.447
We need to start by rebuilding the forge.

05:46.447 --> 05:49.437
The Mero Company might come back.

05:53.417 --> 05:54.667
Rabbit...

05:55.257 --> 05:58.297
I assume things are 
proceeding with that forge?

05:58.927 --> 05:59.787
Yes.

05:59.787 --> 06:02.137
Everything is in place.

06:02.137 --> 06:04.387
Why is it taking so damn long?

06:04.387 --> 06:07.137
Get some thugs together 
and go smash the place up!

06:07.137 --> 06:10.947
Earl Steim, the local lord, 
would likely not appreciate that.

06:10.947 --> 06:14.927
We must avoid damaging the
Mero Company's reputation.

06:16.077 --> 06:17.257
Well, whatever.

06:17.257 --> 06:20.087
So? It's going to work, right?

06:21.587 --> 06:23.907
I've hired the right man.

06:24.227 --> 06:26.957
A man with a golden tongue.

06:33.447 --> 06:35.997
That new guy beat Veil's gang?

06:36.647 --> 06:39.007
He just looks like a kid to me.

06:39.007 --> 06:41.497
No, he's impressive.

06:41.497 --> 06:43.727
Though he looks daft, I'll admit.

06:43.727 --> 06:44.847
Hey!

06:45.177 --> 06:46.717
I can hear you!

06:46.717 --> 06:48.857
Oh, did you see this?

06:50.177 --> 06:52.687
A Mero Company recruitment poster?

06:52.687 --> 06:56.827
They're going to hire 
us at their new store.

06:56.827 --> 06:58.987
The pay's better than I thought, and...

07:04.677 --> 07:05.697
Um...

07:06.207 --> 07:07.317
I've heard the Mero Company

07:07.317 --> 07:10.867
bought the rights to all 
your businesses for a song.

07:11.197 --> 07:13.377
Did they force you to agree to it?

07:13.907 --> 07:16.877
<i>He's a player, just like me.</i>

07:16.877 --> 07:18.757
Shut up, outsider!

07:18.757 --> 07:20.887
Are you spying for them?!

07:20.887 --> 07:23.827
No, no, I'm on your side.

07:23.827 --> 07:26.677
But everyone's looking for workers.

07:27.027 --> 07:30.097
If you were to work for a big 
place like the Mero Company,

07:30.097 --> 07:32.597
you'd have a lot less money worries.

07:33.017 --> 07:34.347
Th-That's...

07:35.107 --> 07:36.107
He's right!

07:36.497 --> 07:38.397
It's the same with this forge.

07:38.757 --> 07:41.277
Even if the Mero Company did take it over,

07:41.277 --> 07:43.257
it would only change who owned it.

07:43.257 --> 07:44.317
<i>What is...</i>

07:43.687 --> 07:48.157
If you're still the ones doing the actual 
work, nobody would lose anything.

07:45.617 --> 07:46.947
<i>this strange feeling?</i>

07:49.777 --> 07:52.617
For an outsider, you've taken
quite the interest in this.

07:52.617 --> 07:53.667
What's your name?

07:54.637 --> 07:55.427
Huroi.

07:55.837 --> 07:57.417
My name is Huroi.

07:57.417 --> 07:58.497
Huroi.

07:58.497 --> 08:03.047
Maybe you're right, and co-existing with 
a larger organization is a good thing.

08:03.047 --> 08:06.297
But in this village, there's 
such a thing as peasant rights.

08:06.297 --> 08:08.087
Peasant rights?

08:08.087 --> 08:12.637
A law for us that was created 
by our lord, Earl Steim.

08:12.857 --> 08:14.777
The locals have the 
right to get information

08:14.777 --> 08:17.647
about the local area 
sooner than anyone else.

08:17.947 --> 08:22.147
Any information that could benefit 
us, we're guaranteed to see.

08:22.397 --> 08:26.197
The earl puts our lives first.

08:26.657 --> 08:31.577
But the Mero Company came here and worked 
with the lord's representative to keep

08:31.577 --> 08:33.377
all the information to themselves.

08:33.377 --> 08:36.247
That goes against the wishes of the earl.

08:36.997 --> 08:39.167
That cannot be allowed.

08:40.407 --> 08:41.907
I see.

08:42.627 --> 08:47.667
Then I shall go to the earl and 
tell him of the company's misdeeds!

08:47.667 --> 08:51.387
If what you're saying is found to 
be true, things should get better!

08:51.387 --> 08:53.587
Th-That would be wonderful!

08:53.587 --> 08:55.807
Please! Help us!

08:55.807 --> 08:59.557
Hmm... You seem to be 
a splendid young man.

09:00.397 --> 09:01.787
<i>I knew it.</i>

09:02.247 --> 09:05.147
<i>He's a player, but he's 
controlling the NPCs.</i>

09:05.877 --> 09:10.177
<i>Did he create a quest and 
change things on his own?</i>

09:14.997 --> 09:15.927
Hey!

09:18.037 --> 09:19.087
What's wrong?

09:19.677 --> 09:23.337
You were clearly working for the 
Mero Company from the start.

09:23.577 --> 09:25.907
How'd you create another quest?

09:26.347 --> 09:29.047
Oh, you noticed, huh?

09:29.047 --> 09:30.717
Get to the point!

09:31.027 --> 09:32.347
Okay, okay.

09:32.347 --> 09:36.637
I decided there was more in it 
for me if I helped the villagers,

09:36.637 --> 09:39.147
and took advantage of this game's freedom.

09:39.547 --> 09:44.647
If you get involved in NPCs' lives, 
it can sometimes trigger a hidden quest.

09:44.647 --> 09:46.027
Like this.

09:46.417 --> 09:48.137
Share quest information.

09:50.657 --> 09:53.077
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65</b>

09:50.657 --> 09:53.077
<b></b>Hidden Quest
 <b>For the Villagers of Winston (A)</b>

You have abandoned the Mero Company's quest
 to persuade the villagers and promised to go to the
capital "Frontier" to tell Earl Steim of their misdeeds.

Clear Condition: Fend off the Company's
attacks and meet with Earl Steim.
 Clear Reward: Title "Apostle of Justice"
 Apostle of Justice: "Courage" stat is unlocked.
All stats +10. Skill "Unyielding Justice" earned.
 Failure: Be caught by the Mero Company.

Level -1
 Banned from Winston until a new lord takes over.

09:51.057 --> 09:52.807
Th-That reward's insane!

09:52.807 --> 09:54.827
I didn't know you could do that!

09:55.877 --> 09:57.807
Of course you wouldn't know it.

09:57.807 --> 10:01.117
Only the game's earliest 
users know about it.

10:01.117 --> 10:04.497
Huh?! I started playing 
at release too, you know!

10:04.497 --> 10:06.797
Do you know how much I've
spent on this damn game?!

10:08.627 --> 10:09.877
You're hilarious!

10:09.877 --> 10:11.967
Shut up! Screw you!

10:11.967 --> 10:16.117
I'd love to be friends, 
but I have something to do now.

10:16.117 --> 10:17.007
See you around!

10:17.517 --> 10:18.957
I never want to see you again!

10:18.957 --> 10:20.537
Get lost!

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 55 0 55 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 30 0 30 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>m 0 0 l 30 0 30 8 0 8</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>Huroi</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>Job: Orator</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>Rarity: Rare</b>

10:22.877 --> 10:24.517
<b>Title: None</b>

10:26.207 --> 10:29.297
I'm going to clear this quest 
no matter what it takes!

10:41.777 --> 10:45.167
You're wasting your time 
visiting Earl Steim.

10:47.177 --> 10:53.637
Didn't I ask you to persuade Kahn and 
the villagers and get that forge?

10:56.157 --> 10:59.737
I was just pretending to 
agree to their request.

10:59.737 --> 11:02.897
Part of brainwashing is making people 
feel at ease with you, right?

11:03.827 --> 11:06.147
A poor excuse, coming from you.

11:08.967 --> 11:11.617
Let's lock this traitor up.

11:11.987 --> 11:14.257
Take him to the underground prison.

11:20.347 --> 11:22.337
How'd he know?

11:23.207 --> 11:27.907
My first secret quest, 
and this is how it fails?

11:27.907 --> 11:31.257
<i>System guidance. The quest has changed.</i>

11:31.967 --> 11:34.137
<i>Your new quest is "Waiting (S)."</i>

11:33.257 --> 11:39.017
<b></b>Hidden Quest
<b>Waiting (S)</b>


The Mero Company has locked you
in Winston Castle's underground prison.
If you can endure your endless wait
in the inescapable prison, the "Apostle of Justice"
that you failed to become will save you!


Clear Condition: Don't log out for
8 days of in-game time.
*This is an extremely dangerous quest.
Elderly players or players with health concerns,
please abandon the quest.


Clear Reward: Second job
"Partner of the Apostle of Justice"
*Stat "Courage" unlocked.
All stats +20 when with the Apostle of Justice.
Skills "Unyielding Justice" + "Sacrifice for Justice"
Title "He Who Has Surpassed a Trial"
*Stat "Indomitability" unlocked
Skill "Strong Will"


Failure: No penalty

11:33.257 --> 11:39.017
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 106 0 106</b>

11:34.137 --> 11:35.847
The quest changed?

11:34.817 --> 11:37.827
<i>This quest is extremely dangerous.</i>

11:36.447 --> 11:39.017
This is the real hidden quest?

11:37.827 --> 11:41.827
<i>If you are concerned about your physical 
condition, please abandon the quest.</i>

11:39.637 --> 11:43.157
Eight days?! That's fifty hours real-time!

11:43.857 --> 11:47.377
The most I've ever been 
able to do is twenty!

11:48.427 --> 11:49.677
Fifty hours...

11:50.037 --> 11:52.657
If anything abnormal 
happens to my brainwaves,

11:53.447 --> 11:55.827
the game will log me out on its own!

11:56.817 --> 11:58.777
And then I'll have nothing!

11:59.967 --> 12:01.117
<b><b>Will you abandon the quest?</b></b>

12:07.877 --> 12:10.377
<b><b>Will you abandon the quest?</b></b>

12:14.377 --> 12:16.607
<b><b>Will you abandon the quest?</b></b>

12:16.447 --> 12:17.677
<b><b>Quest Received</b></b>

12:16.447 --> 12:17.677
<b><b>Time Remaining</b></b>

12:18.287 --> 12:20.737
I'll clear this quest no matter what!

12:22.177 --> 12:24.827
I'm waiting, Apostle of Justice!

12:30.037 --> 12:32.307
Quest B408 has begun.

12:32.657 --> 12:34.987
We will begin an emergency
board meeting.

12:34.987 --> 12:36.907
<b><b>Time Remaining</b></b>

12:37.537 --> 12:39.407
B408 is...

12:39.627 --> 12:44.167
An S-rank hidden quest that only 
appears under special conditions?

12:44.167 --> 12:44.857
Yes.

12:44.857 --> 12:47.917
If it is completed, 
it will result in the birth

12:48.367 --> 12:51.297
of the first <i>Satisfy</i> user with two jobs.

12:51.717 --> 12:55.437
Until now, people have 
been focused on rare jobs.

12:55.777 --> 13:00.507
But that will change once the 
existence of second jobs is known.

13:01.217 --> 13:05.927
This quest has a great deal 
of meaning to <i>Satisfy</i>.

13:09.827 --> 13:14.537
The ID of the player attempting 
Quest 408B is Huroi.

13:14.897 --> 13:17.607
His real name is Damb Allunbatar.

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Profile

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Huroi

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Registration Date

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Gender

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Male

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Job

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Orator

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Affiliation

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
None

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Weapon

13:14.897 --> 13:19.907
Dagger

13:17.607 --> 13:22.937
A 24-year old Mongolian user, 
he is currently a level 126 Orator.

13:23.407 --> 13:26.667
His longest continuous login 
to date was twenty hours.

13:27.587 --> 13:30.127
There were no abnormalities in his vitals,

13:30.127 --> 13:33.127
but the psychological stress 
was great, it seems.

13:33.127 --> 13:37.127
The capsule's force logout 
was about to trigger.

13:37.807 --> 13:43.387
Given this data, we estimate his chance 
of completing the quest to be 9%.

13:43.797 --> 13:45.127
Too low.

13:45.127 --> 13:47.437
The danger is greater...

13:47.687 --> 13:51.457
In addition, the "Apostle of Justice" 
whose job it is to save Huroi

13:51.457 --> 13:53.947
is supposed to be an NPC, but...

13:53.947 --> 13:55.697
A variable appeared?

13:55.697 --> 13:57.467
This accident is...

13:57.987 --> 14:01.047
It appears that the user 
he shared the quest with

14:01.047 --> 14:04.487
will be treated as the Apostle of Justice.

14:04.787 --> 14:07.727
Though the person himself 
hasn't realized it.

14:08.457 --> 14:12.907
But can he save Huroi in the dungeon?

14:09.727 --> 14:12.257
Brother, you're going to catch a cold.

14:12.257 --> 14:13.497
Ew, I can smell the beer!

14:13.497 --> 14:17.757
Looking at the direction this NPC went,

14:18.057 --> 14:19.937
we can develop a theory.

14:20.897 --> 14:26.267
The key to this is likely 
the third epic job bearer.

14:29.387 --> 14:30.757
A coincidence...

14:30.757 --> 14:33.817
I don't really believe in them.

14:34.247 --> 14:36.667
But if this works, 
I'll take advantage of it.

14:44.257 --> 14:46.697
Eternal Kingdom, Earl Steim's Territory

14:44.257 --> 14:46.697
Akero Dungeon

14:47.137 --> 14:49.137
Please join our party!

14:49.137 --> 14:51.377
No, join ours!

14:51.377 --> 14:52.787
Please!

14:52.787 --> 14:54.737
Euphemina-san!

14:54.737 --> 14:56.937
Okay...

14:56.937 --> 15:04.677
Please show me what you all can do, then!

15:06.307 --> 15:08.827
Euphemina-san belongs to us!

15:08.827 --> 15:10.687
No, us!

15:11.097 --> 15:13.187
Explosive Veil!

15:13.187 --> 15:15.187
Lightning Slice!

15:16.227 --> 15:17.717
Hmm...

15:17.717 --> 15:20.697
Not quite as good as I thought.

15:22.857 --> 15:26.277
Frenzied Spiral!

15:28.177 --> 15:29.747
Not bad.

15:33.177 --> 15:34.547
<i>Skill Copy.</i>

15:44.397 --> 15:46.257
<i>Your Skill Copy was successful.</i>

15:46.257 --> 15:50.267
<b>Frenzied Spiral</b>

15:46.257 --> 15:50.267
<b>Uses</b>

15:46.257 --> 15:50.267
<b></b>Creates a spiral for 5 seconds.

15:46.257 --> 15:50.267
<b></b>Does 1,530-2,380 damage per second to enemies in its radius. Agility 80% down.

15:46.257 --> 15:50.267
<b></b>This skill was copied with Skill Copy. It can be stored until you use it.

15:47.247 --> 15:49.707
<i>You can use this skill once.</i>

15:51.517 --> 15:53.987
<i>This is the power of an epic job.</i>

15:57.117 --> 15:59.927
Well? Will you join our party now...

16:00.577 --> 16:02.517
Euphemina-san?

16:03.277 --> 16:07.277
<b></b>Quest
<b>Condemn the Red Knight Traitor (S)</b>


The Saharan Empire's Red Knights
are the continent's strongest.
The former knight commander, Piaro,
who betrayed and badly injured
the current knight commander, Asmophel,
is hiding in Kesan Canyon.
Asmophel has asked you to take revenge.


Clear Condition: Find and condemn Piaro

16:03.277 --> 16:07.277
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 52 0 52</b>

16:03.887 --> 16:06.797
Condemn the Red Knight Traitor (S).

16:07.277 --> 16:10.477
Find and condemn the former 
knight commander, Piaro.

16:11.537 --> 16:14.787
I think I'm going to be able 
to take on this S-rank quest.

16:16.927 --> 16:18.627
What do <i>you</i> want?

16:18.847 --> 16:21.577
You were staring at me from 
a long way away, weren't you?

16:22.567 --> 16:25.337
You don't remember me?

16:26.407 --> 16:28.387
I'm not going on a date with you.

16:28.387 --> 16:31.017
Do you remember the name Erina?

16:31.977 --> 16:37.367
She was hired by the Mero Company 
for her incredible talents,

16:37.367 --> 16:40.167
but vanished after taking the advance.

16:40.167 --> 16:43.237
A blacksmith... no.

16:43.647 --> 16:46.487
Euphemina the Duplicator.

16:50.237 --> 16:53.437
None of the users know yet.

16:53.437 --> 16:55.567
You know 'cause you're an NPC, huh?

16:56.097 --> 16:58.757
I can't answer that.

16:59.347 --> 17:02.097
But I do wonder: what's your hurry?

17:03.437 --> 17:07.337
I'm actually dealing with a tough quest.

17:07.847 --> 17:10.747
The strongest knight of 
the Saharan Empire, Piaro.

17:11.347 --> 17:14.077
I have to beat him.

17:15.827 --> 17:19.267
I'm sorry, but you're going 
to have to abandon that quest.

17:19.267 --> 17:20.197
What?

17:20.197 --> 17:23.147
I'd like your help with another quest.

17:24.107 --> 17:26.357
<b></b>Quest

17:24.107 --> 17:26.357
<b><b>Item Creation Match (Unknown)</b></b>

17:24.887 --> 17:26.357
Difficulty unknown?

17:26.357 --> 17:27.497
Correct.

17:27.497 --> 17:29.817
You're an NPC, and you're threatening me?

17:29.817 --> 17:34.627
But these conditions are 
good for you, aren't they?

17:32.117 --> 17:34.997
<b></b>Clear Condition: Win the Item Creation Match
Clear Reward: 1,500 gold
Title "Player of Games"
Player of Games: Stats "Fighting Spirit" "Luck"
Skill "Roll the Dice"...

17:32.117 --> 17:34.997
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 23 0 23</b>

17:39.387 --> 17:40.957
Huroi was arrested?

17:40.957 --> 17:41.997
Yes.

17:41.997 --> 17:44.957
Under suspicion of treason 
against Earl Steim.

17:44.957 --> 17:48.587
He's being kept in the castle's 
underground prison right now.

17:49.317 --> 17:51.097
Is that...

17:51.097 --> 17:55.297
Yes, it looks like the Mero Company 
has someone smart working for them.

18:00.607 --> 18:02.147
Excuse me.

18:02.147 --> 18:05.107
I am Rabbit of the Mero Company.

18:05.617 --> 18:08.877
I've come on behalf of my master, Valmont.

18:12.867 --> 18:17.757
In other words, if we want to free Huroi, 
we have to agree to your proposal?

18:18.117 --> 18:19.827
Correct.

18:19.897 --> 18:21.137
Ha! As if.

18:21.137 --> 18:23.127
I don't care what happens to that guy.

18:23.457 --> 18:25.677
How heartless.

18:25.677 --> 18:29.857
Whatever his reasons, he tried 
to protect the villagers.

18:30.917 --> 18:33.767
He went to see the earl, 
regardless of the danger.

18:33.767 --> 18:36.057
You're going to just abandon him?

18:38.467 --> 18:43.017
Of course, I'm not asking you to hand 
over the forge just for his freedom.

18:44.807 --> 18:48.737
I want you to have an 
item-crafting match with us.

18:48.737 --> 18:49.727
What?

18:49.727 --> 18:54.147
If you win, we'll give up on the forge.

18:54.147 --> 18:56.547
And we'll release Huroi.

18:57.827 --> 18:58.967
Very well.

18:59.327 --> 19:02.497
But I won't participate. 
It will be the successor...

19:02.777 --> 19:05.497
Pagma's Successor.

19:06.247 --> 19:07.757
Pagma's Successor?

19:07.757 --> 19:09.257
Grid here.

19:09.257 --> 19:12.297
Hey! Who said you could—

19:10.737 --> 19:12.297
<i>System guidance.</i>

19:12.297 --> 19:16.967
<i>Quest "Item Creation Match with the 
Mero Company" has been generated.</i>

19:16.967 --> 19:19.917
600 gold?!

19:18.337 --> 19:19.717
<i>Will you accept it?</i>

19:21.977 --> 19:23.507
<i>Quest accepted.</i>

19:23.507 --> 19:26.897
Come and get me, you four-eyed weirdo!

19:26.897 --> 19:28.417
Of course.

19:28.417 --> 19:34.157
I'll prove that you're lying 
about being Pagma's Successor.

19:34.157 --> 19:41.157
<b></b>Quest
<b>Item Creation Match
with the Mero Company (Unknown)</b>


The Mero Company has challenged you
in a battle for the forge.
Kahn is in poor shape and has asked you
to participate in his stead.


Clear Condition: Win the Mero Company's match
Clear Reward: 600 gold prize
+500 fame in Winston

Failure: Fame in Winston becomes 1.
Kahn loses his forge to the Mero Company.

19:34.157 --> 19:41.157
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 62 0 62</b>

19:34.397 --> 19:37.387
The match will be in three days.
Is that acceptable?

19:36.567 --> 19:38.447
Yeah, I'll kick your ass!

19:38.447 --> 19:41.157
That 72,000 yen is mine!

19:44.417 --> 19:48.917
<b></b>Quest

19:44.417 --> 19:48.917
<b><b>Waiting</b></b>

19:44.417 --> 19:48.917
<b><b>Time Remaining</b></b>

19:49.217 --> 19:51.887
I'm finally... halfway there...

19:55.057 --> 19:56.797
I'm gonna do this.

19:57.297 --> 20:00.507
I won't give in... no matter what...

20:02.917 --> 20:04.327
<i>Don't underestimate me!</i>

20:04.327 --> 20:07.067
<i>I'm the legendary blacksmith!</i>

20:07.567 --> 20:11.277
<i>I'll show you what a 
legendary job can do!</i>

20:15.277 --> 20:17.377
Hello, everyone!

20:17.377 --> 20:24.787
Thank you for gathering for the 
Mero Company's Item Match event!

20:26.787 --> 20:30.797
Now, let's introduce our two challengers!

20:31.067 --> 20:33.207
We can really win this, right?

20:33.207 --> 20:34.427
Of course.

20:35.137 --> 20:38.177
From Kahn's forge... Grid!

20:38.177 --> 20:39.667
You can do it, Grid!

20:39.667 --> 20:41.177
Protect the forge!

20:41.647 --> 20:44.467
From the Mero Company... Erina!

20:48.057 --> 20:50.457
Thanks for the support, everyone!

20:54.817 --> 21:00.287
Erina! Erina! Erina!

20:58.817 --> 20:59.777
Screw you!

21:01.277 --> 21:05.787
This tournament will 
determine Huroi's fate.

21:06.297 --> 21:09.847
Hinako-kun, are we in touch with 
<i>Satisfy</i>'s Mongolian branch?

21:10.197 --> 21:10.797
Yes.

21:11.297 --> 21:15.797
Local staff are on standby, 
ready to grab Huroi if necessary.

21:17.537 --> 21:20.877
Now, whether Quest B408—that is,

21:18.297 --> 21:24.617
<b><b>Time Remaining</b></b>

21:20.877 --> 21:24.617
<i>Satisfy</i>'s first-ever 
second job, will be born...

21:25.457 --> 21:27.587
<i>depends on Grid.</i>

21:28.007 --> 21:29.287
Grid-san!

21:30.327 --> 21:32.447
Nice to meet you!

21:33.377 --> 21:35.567
Don't get all friendly with me, brat.

21:36.587 --> 21:39.187
I'm nineteen years old.

21:39.187 --> 21:40.907
I'm not a kid!

21:40.907 --> 21:43.787
Well, you're more of a kid than I am!

21:43.787 --> 21:44.907
You're really annoying.

21:44.907 --> 21:46.367
No, you are, shrimp!

21:51.467 --> 21:53.757
W-Wait, both of you!

21:55.037 --> 21:56.257
Now...

21:56.257 --> 21:58.357
Let the match begin!
